What was fixed (commit `359c0378`, "fix(yang.php): the provenance dates and the JSON depth/number scanner"):

1. Provenance dates — `test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`. Five records (`gc_013`, `gc_023`, `bug39438`, `bug64660`, `gc_012`) cited `{:tree "06cd429f" :date "2026-11-04"}`, but `06cd429f` committed 2026-11-06, so the pair is impossible. The results came from the Nov-4 oracle pass (manifest regenerated in `2e5f7f2f` on 2026-11-04) whose exact shiva checkout hash was never recorded, so per the brief no hash was invented: all five now carry `:tree "unrecorded"`, keeping the supported date, host, and log. `bug40809` keeps its correct `dbe9e072`/2026-11-05 remeasure record. Re-validated: 6 gaps, 6 measured via `clojure.edn`. No code reads `:measured-at`.
2. JSON depth off-by-one — `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc`, `php/json-encode`: guard changed from `(>= (+ depth 1) maxdepth)` to `(> (+ depth 1) maxdepth)`, so `json_encode([1],0,1)` → `"[1]"` while `json_encode([[1]],0,1)` → `false`. Test pin corrected to `string(3) "[1]"` (diag still `[]`), plus a new `[[1]]` → `false` pin.
